{
  "label": "Comms Deck",
  "order": 2,
  "$description": "A ship's comms console. Agents are channels on a jack field, and each pending Round is a lit channel lamp. Worn bakelite keys, enamel panels with screw heads and stencilled plates carry the identity; Round strips, Questions and attachments stay opaque paper and code planes.",
  "signature": "Answering patches the channel, and the lamp goes dark. When an Answer is sent, a patch cord seats in the channel jack and the lit lamp fades out: on the Answered toast, on the newest answered-log row and on the phone's sent screen. Pending lamps stay lit while a Round waits; answered badges keep the seated plug.",
  "colorScheme": "dark",
  "palette": {
    "label": "Bakelite Olive"
  },
